<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Society on AI and Society Course</title><link>https://msu-cerl.github.io/cmse101/tags/society/</link><description>Recent content in Society on AI and Society Course</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://msu-cerl.github.io/cmse101/tags/society/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>AI and Society Course</title><link>https://msu-cerl.github.io/cmse101/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://msu-cerl.github.io/cmse101/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="ai-and-society"&gt;AI and Society&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Hybrid/HyFlex Course on AI and Its Societal Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-course-description"&gt;📘 Course Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This course explores the multifaceted relationships between artificial intelligence and contemporary society. Students examine AI&amp;rsquo;s applications, limitations, and implications across ethics, policy, economics, employment, and social justice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through readings, discussions, and projects, we critically analyze how these technologies shape—and are shaped by—our lives, values, and societies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-course-format"&gt;📚 Course Format&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid/HyFlex:&lt;/strong&gt; Readings and materials available on this site and via D2L Brightspace. Attend in person or participate remotely—your choice.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Assignments</title><link>https://msu-cerl.github.io/cmse101/assignments/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://msu-cerl.github.io/cmse101/assignments/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="-course-assignments"&gt;📝 Course Assignments&lt;/h2&gt;
